        <mxCell id="why" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;strokeColor=#999999;fillColor=#ffffff;fontColor=#000000;spacing=8;" value="&lt;b&gt;Why ECS Fargate?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Serverless: no servers or nodes to patch&lt;br&gt;- Simpler than EKS for one API + one worker&lt;br&gt;- Works natively with ALB, IAM roles and Secrets Manager&lt;br&gt;- API and worker: 2 tasks each, spread across both AZs" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="112" width="410" x="20" y="560" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;strokeColor=#999999;fillColor=#ffffff;fontColor=#000000;spacing=8;" value="&lt;b&gt;Request flow (browser to database and back)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. User opens shopyyy.com; Route 53 (DNS 53) answers with the CloudFront alias&lt;br&gt;2. Browser connects to CloudFront over HTTPS 443 (ACM certificate)&lt;br&gt;3a. /* goes to the S3 bucket (React files) over 443, read through OAC&lt;br&gt;3b. /api/* goes to api.shopyyy.com -&amp;gt; Internet Gateway -&amp;gt; ALB (443, secret origin header)&lt;br&gt;4. ALB forwards to the ECS Fargate API tasks in the private subnets (port 3000)&lt;br&gt;5. API checks ElastiCache Redis (6379) for cached product listings&lt;br&gt;6. On a cache miss the API reads/writes RDS PostgreSQL (5432, Multi-AZ)&lt;br&gt;7. New order: the API publishes a message to Kafka on MSK (9092)&lt;br&gt;8. Worker consumes the message from MSK (9092)&lt;br&gt;9. Worker saves the order in RDS PostgreSQL (5432)&lt;br&gt;10. Response returns the same way: RDS/Redis -&amp;gt; API -&amp;gt; ALB -&amp;gt; CloudFront -&amp;gt; browser" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="200" width="660" x="20" y="880" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sgbox" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;strokeColor=#999999;fillColor=#ffffff;fontColor=#000000;spacing=8;" value="&lt;b&gt;Security Groups (who can talk to whom) - red dashed boxes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;ALB SG: &lt;/b&gt;inbound 443 from CloudFront (AWS managed prefix list); outbound 3000 to ECS SG&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;ECS SG (API + worker): &lt;/b&gt;inbound 3000 from ALB SG only; outbound 5432 to RDS SG, 6379 to Redis SG, 9092 to MSK SG, and 443 to the internet via NAT (image pull, Secrets Manager)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;RDS SG: &lt;/b&gt;inbound 5432 from ECS SG only&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Redis SG: &lt;/b&gt;inbound 6379 from ECS SG only&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;MSK SG: &lt;/b&gt;inbound 9092 from ECS SG only&lt;br&gt;Private subnets reach the internet (updates, image pulls) only through the NAT Gateway." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="200" width="700" x="700" y="880" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e1" edge="1" parent="1" source="users" target="r53" style="html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=classic;endFill=1;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=1.5;exitX=0.5;exitY=0.0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;exitPerimeter=0;entryX=0.3023;entryY=1.0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryPerimeter=0;">
